Expected elements: present

All must-show items render and no must-not-show item appears: nav with resolver, breadcrumb `Home / aztec / tx / 0x14d6…fa6c`, full hash, `Succeeded`, the neutral `Not observable` badge with the published pruning reason, a six-row Overview, all four content sections each stating a permanent absence, footer with the three marks drawn and the disclosure. The `Data` row carrying `Real Aztec mainnet data` is the sole provenance marker and lands first. No debug/retry/spinner, no trace reference, no error tone.

Iteration changes, all landed: base-ten cost (`3906250659561864576 mana (FeeJuice)`, not a hex word); the three-state decoded-input note (the "no call data" arm renders, no false selector claim); labelled `Age` (`No timestamp published`) and `Type` rows; the provenance note flush-left in a grid-spanning `dd` (x≈530, aligned to the label column); the `/aztec` route.

Change (2) exposed a defect one row above it. `RAW 0x` (y≈1520) renders unknown as empty bytes while the note 40px below says this section cannot tell whether none was published or the body was pruned, and the Raw JSON (y≈2530) says `"bodyRetainedAtCapture": false`. `SELECTOR` uses `—` for the same unknown. That is my first finding, P1, rating capped at 4.

The page otherwise reads as correct, not broken. Density is the weak axis: the capture paragraph (y 805–1045) is 45% of the Overview grid, ahead of every fact.

Fixes: render `RAW` as `—`; move the capture telemetry out of the first grid row.

Rating: 4/10

